window.MONSTER_CHUNK_87 = [{"name":"Kakuen-taka","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","evil","extraplanar","swarm"],"init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":9,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +1 dodge, +1 natural, -2 size","hp":199,"hd":"21d10+84","hdvalue":21,"fort":17,"ref":20,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["fleshy shield"],"immunities":["poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"swarm (5d6 plus dimensional snare and distraction), 2 slams +19 (5d6)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"0 ft. (10 ft. with slam)","special_attacks":[{"type":"consume flesh"},{"type":"trample","details":"5d6, DC 20"}],"strength":10,"dexterity":23,"constitution":16,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":13,"charisma":13,"baseatk":21,"cmb":23,"cmd":40,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (consume flesh)"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Iron Will"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Run"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Step Up"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":30},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":31},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Survival","value":11}],"languages":["Abyssal"],"environments":["any (the Worldwound)"],"organizations":["solitary","patrol (1 swarm with 1 flesh mansion and 1d4 carrionstorms)","gang (1d3 patrols)"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"Within a towering structure of bone and rotting flesh lurk hundreds of flittering fiends.","source":"Inner Sea Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Consume Flesh","kind":"Su","details":"Once per round, when a kakuen-taka kills or reduces a creature to negative hit points with its swarm attack, it automatically attempts to consume the target's flesh as a free action (Fortitude DC 24 negates). If the target fails its save, its body is destroyed and the kakuen-taka gains the benefits of a death knell spell. This is a death attack."},{"type":"Create Carrionstorm","kind":"Ex","details":"As a full-round action at sunrise, a kakuen-taka (a bhoga swarm with a flesh mansion) can create 1d4 carrionstorms. These carrionstorms have a blinding poison in addition to their swarm attack. The carrionstorms are not under the control of the kakuen-taka but instinctively follow it, attacking minor foes while the kakuen-taka destroys greater threats. If the flesh mansion is destroyed and the kakuen-taka doesn't create another one within 24 hours, the carrionstorms are destroyed. Any carrionstorms in excess of four wander away from the kakuen-taka and are automatically destroyed 24 hours later."},{"type":"Carrionstorm Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Swarm-injury; save Fort DC 12, frequency 1/round for 6 rounds, effect permanent blindness, cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based (using the carrionstorm's Constitution)."},{"type":"Dimensional Snare","kind":"Su","details":"Any creature affected by the kakuen-taka's swarm attack must succeed at a DC 21 Will save or be affected by dimensional anchor for 1 round. This save is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Flesh Mansion","kind":"Ex","details":"A kakuen-taka's bhoga swarm normally inhabits a hollowed-out reconfigured corpse called a flesh mansion, which it uses as a shelter, vehicle, and war machine. When the swarm wears a flesh mansion, it uses the above stat block (unlike a normal swarm, the flesh mansion's slam attacks have reach and threaten squares within its reach). As a standard action, the swarm can abandon its flesh mansion (which falls inert in its square), inhabit an empty flesh mansion, hide within its flesh mansion (gaining cover against all opponents but still being able to use its swarm attack), or stop hiding within the flesh mansion. If the flesh mansion is destroyed, the swarm can create another by performing a ritual that requires 1 hour and the corpse of a Huge creature. The flesh mansion isn't a separate creature, nor is it undead; it is merely a corpse the swarm manipulates. Without a flesh mansion, the bhoga swarm's statistics are CE Diminutive outsider (chaotic, evil, extraplanar, swarm); AC 22, touch 21, flat-footed 15; Defensive Abilities swarm traits; Melee swarm (5d6 plus dimensional snare and distraction); Reach 0 ft.; Str 1; CMB -; CMD - (can't be tripped); Stealth +32."},{"type":"Fleshy Shield","kind":"Ex","details":"A newly created flesh mansion has 150 hit points. The swarm takes only half damage from all attacks that deal hit point damage, with the remainder taken by the flesh mansion. Because a swarm of Diminutive creatures is immune to all weapon damage, apply half of all weapon damage to the fleshy shield and ignore the half that would be applied to the swarm. When the flesh mansion reaches 0 hit points, it is destroyed and the swarm functions like a normal swarm (see Flesh Mansion above). A kakuen-taka can repair a damaged flesh mansion by spending a full-round action grafting a corpse into it (restoring 5 hit points for a Small corpse, 10 for Medium, 20 for Large, 50 for Huge)."}],"description":"In the far northern lands bordering on the Worldwound, a strange and terrifying menace plagues the tundra and prairie-shambling fleshy abominations called kakuen-taka, the Hunger That Moves. They wander the desolate emptiness of the subpolar wilds, a living manifestation of the Worldwound's taint whose horrific onset is presaged by a sour-sweet wind and wheeling, screaming flocks of undead birds. The lucky victims of the birds' blinding poison are spared the sight of the rumbling juggernauts of putrefying meat driven like siege engines by a swarm of fiends called bhogas. Individually these fiends have little wit or skill, but together they have a malign intellect that allows them to construct mobile nests out of dead flesh like morbid termites building a mound.\n\nThe bhogas find a giant, mammoth, or other creature of great size and devour its organs, usually while the creature is still alive and trying to resist. Once the creature is dying or dead, the fiends reconfigure the corpse's remaining flesh and bone into a hideous, multilegged pillar, which they then invade and inhabit like a hollow tree. Some of the bhogas use their collective strength to move the fleshy mansion's limbs while the rest clamber about its walls or skulk underneath it, searching for new prey to terrorize and consume. This monstrosity attracts birds the fiends animate as flesh-craving undead swarms. Together, the three components of this peculiar Ecology stalk the demon-tainted lands. If a healthy swarm discovers another suitable corpse, the fiends engage in a frenzy of mating, build a second flesh mansion, split into two swarms, then rapidly give birth to fill all the available space in their new home.\n\nWhen a flesh mansion becomes so rotted that it cannot maintain its structure or the swarm cannot easily move it, the bhogas abandon their creation and seek out another, leaving behind a monstrous, decaying shell, unrecognizable as the living creature it once was. Necromancers can use the husk for parts or animate the entire thing as a new abomination. Desperate ghouls, zombies, or animals might feed on it and become tainted by its latent Abyssal energies.\n\nAs much a plague upon demons as upon the mortal races, kakuen-taka have no true allies. Perhaps this accounts for their constant wandering and their fondness for desolate and isolated locales, far from any that might interfere with their feasting. Rarely, a powerful demon might enslave one with magic and use the swarm's dimensional snare ability to capture and kill its rivals. Driven out of the central part of the Worldwound by more intelligent and organized demons, kakuen-taka have become a recurring plague in the southern fringes of the territory, below Storasta and abutting the borders with Numeria and Ustalav. In these lonely moors and hills, kakuen-taka regularly eradicate patrols and entire settlements. None of the adjacent countries values the empty lands highly enough to risk major resources to stamp them out.\n\nKakuen-taka are indifferent to their own kind and attack each other only if one swarm has a flesh mansion and the other doesn't. Given adequate food, several kakuen-taka might travel together to tear apart larger prey, but over time they usually wander apart, following their separate carrionstorms, and have no sense of loyalty toward their former comrades.","ecology":"stalk the demon-tainted lands. If a healthy swarm discovers another suitable corpse, the fiends engage in a frenzy of mating, build a second flesh mansion, split into two swarms, then rapidly give birth to fill all the available space in their new home.\n\nWhen a flesh mansion becomes so rotted that it cannot maintain its structure or the swarm cannot easily move it, the bhogas abandon their creation and seek out another, leaving behind a monstrous, decaying shell, unrecognizable as the living creature it once was. Necromancers can use the husk for parts or animate the entire thing as a new abomination. Desperate ghouls, zombies, or animals might feed on it and become tainted by its latent Abyssal energies.\n\nAs much a plague upon demons as upon the mortal races, kakuen-taka have no true allies. Perhaps this accounts for their constant wandering and their fondness for desolate and isolated locales, far from any that might interfere with their feasting. Rarely, a powerful demon might enslave one with magic and use the swarm's dimensional snare ability to capture and kill its rivals. Driven out of the central part of the Worldwound by more intelligent and organized demons, kakuen-taka have become a recurring plague in the southern fringes of the territory, below Storasta and abutting the borders with Numeria and Ustalav. In these lonely moors and hills, kakuen-taka regularly eradicate patrols and entire settlements. None of the adjacent countries values the empty lands highly enough to risk major resources to stamp them out.\n\nKakuen-taka are indifferent to their own kind and attack each other only if one swarm has a flesh mansion and the other doesn't. Given adequate food, several kakuen-taka might travel together to tear apart larger prey, but over time they usually wander apart, following their separate carrionstorms, and have no sense of loyalty toward their former comrades.","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Leng Spider","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["extraplanar"],"init":13,"senses":[{"type":"arcane sight"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":29,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+9 Dex, +12 natural, -2 size","hp":202,"hd":"15d10+120","hdvalue":15,"hp_mods":["fast healing 10"],"fort":17,"ref":18,"will":10,"immunities":["cold","confusion and insanity effects","poison","sonic"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"climb","speed":40}],"melee":"mwk flail +22 (3d6+8), bite +16 (2d6+4 plus poison)","ranged":"mwk bolas +23 (1d8+8)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"web","details":"+24 ranged, DC 25, 15 hp"},{"type":"web weaponry"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":23,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"arcane sight"},{"spell":"freedom of movement"},{"spell":"tongues"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"fabricate","details":"webs only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"insanity"},{"spell":"mirage arcana"},{"spell":"veil"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"air walk"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"major image"}]}],"strength":26,"dexterity":29,"constitution":26,"intelligence":21,"wisdom":17,"charisma":22,"baseatk":15,"cmb":25,"cmd":44,"cmd_special":"+10 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Trip"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Point-Blank Shot"},{"feat":"Precise Shot"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":27,"special":"+31 jump"},{"skill":"Climb","value":34},{"skill":"Craft (traps)","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (any one)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":21},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":20},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":21}],"languages":["Aklo","tongues"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","cult (3-6)"],"treasure":"double","description_visual":"This immense purple spider has a legspan of nearly forty ft. and a hideously bloated body, yet still moves with fluid grace.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Su","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 25; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Con plus confusion for 1 round; cure 2 consecutive saves. A Leng spider's venom causes flesh to blister and rot away and the mind to experience vivid and horrific hallucinations-these visions cause the poisoned creature to react in an unpredictable manner, as if confused. The hallucination element of this poison is mind-affecting. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Web Weaponry","kind":"Ex","details":"A Leng spider is talented at using its webs to construct masterwork weapons. This technique of weapon creation allows the spider to effectively create a flail or bolas by attaching a heavy object such as a rock or chunk of metal to a cord of webbing. The spider attaches one end of this webbing to a leg and can then wield the weighted cord as a masterwork flail or a masterwork bolas. It can only wield one such weapon at a time-it must use its other legs to walk. If a Leng spider drops or loses a web weapon, it can create a new one as a full-round action, provided it has access to heavy-weight objects of the correct size (such as loose rocks or skulls)."}],"description":"The spiders of Leng have long warred with that realm's more humanoid denizens, yet this doesn't make the spiders allies of sane life. These spiders see themselves as deserving of true positions of power, and the only creatures they suffer to live apart from their kin are their magically controlled slaves. Fortunately, the spiders have no intrinsic way to travel to the Material Plane, and must use portals or other methods to visit this world. Artistic trap builders, Leng spiders construct lairs of dangerous and haunting beauty made of webs and other materials found nearby.\n\nA Leng spider's body is 18 ft. long and weighs 6,000 pounds. Most leng spiders possess only 7 legs, but some possess 9, 11, or only 5-they never possess an even number.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mature Adult Blue Dragon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["electricity (5ft., 1d6 electricity)","frightful presence (210 ft., DC 22)"],"ac":31,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":31,"ac_mods":"+23 natural, -2 size","hp":207,"hd":"18d12+90","hdvalue":18,"fort":16,"ref":11,"will":14,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +26 (2d8+13), 2 claws +25 (2d6+9), 2 wings +23 (1d8+4), tail slap +23 (2d6+13)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 24, 14d8 electricity"},{"type":"crush","details":"Small creatures, DC 24, 2d8+13"},{"type":"desert thirst","details":"DC 24"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":18,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":27,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"minor image"},{"spell":"ventriloquism"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":16,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"vampiric touch"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"darkness"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"resist energy"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"},{"spell":"unseen servant"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane mark"},{"spell":"bleed"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":29,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":18,"cmb":29,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Dazzling Display"},{"feat":"Deadly Stroke"},{"feat":"Extend Spell"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Shatter Defenses"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":24},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Survival","value":24}],"languages":["Auran","Common","Draconic","Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"sound imitation"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"With scales the color of the desert sky, this large, serpentine dragon moves with an unsettling grace.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Desert Thirst","kind":"Su","details":"A blue dragon can cast create water at will (CL 18). Alternatively, it can destroy an equal amount of liquid in a 10-foot burst. Unattended liquids are instantly reduced to sand. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC 24) or be destroyed."},{"type":"Electricity Aura","kind":"Su","details":"A mature adult blue dragon is surrounded by an aura of electricity. Creatures within 5 ft. take 1d6 points of electricity damage at the beginning of the dragon's turn."},{"type":"Sound Imitation","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older blue dragon can mimic any voice or sound it has heard by making a successful Bluff check against a listener's Sense Motive check."}],"description":"Blue dragons are consummate schemers and obsessively orderly. In combat, blue dragons prefer to surprise foes if possible, and are not above retreating if the odds turn against them. They prefer to lair near those that they control, sometimes even within the confines of a city.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mature Adult Bronze Dragon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"LG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (210 ft., DC 24)"],"ac":31,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":31,"ac_mods":"+23 natural, -2 size","hp":207,"hd":"18d12+90","hdvalue":18,"fort":16,"ref":11,"will":16,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +25 (2d8+13), 2 claws +25 (2d6+9), tail slap +23 (2d6+13), 2 wings +23 (1d8+4)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 24, 14d6 electricity"},{"type":"crush","details":"2d8+13, DC 24"},{"type":"repulsion breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":18,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":23,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"create food and water"},{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"speak with animals"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":9,"spellsknown_concentration":14,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"ice storm"},{"spell":"solid fog"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"heroism"},{"spell":"slow"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"gust of wind"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"}]}],"strength":29,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":21,"charisma":20,"baseatk":18,"cmb":29,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":26},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":23},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":26},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":26},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":26},{"skill":"Perception","value":30},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":30},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":26},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Swim","value":38}],"languages":["Aquan","Common","Draconic","Elven","Gnome","1 more"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"animal or humanoid, polymorph"},{"type":"water breathing"},{"type":"wave mastery","details":"70 min"}],"environments":["temperate coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This sleek dragon is covered in dull metallic scales that range in color from shining bronze to mottled blue.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Repulsion Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of electricity, a bronze dragon can breathe a cone of repulsion gas. Targets must make a Will save or be compelled to do nothing but move away from the dragon for 1d6 rounds plus 1 round per age category. This is a mind-affecting compulsion effect."},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A bronze dragon breathes water and can use its breath weapon, spells, and abilities underwater."},{"type":"Wave Mastery","kind":"Su","details":"For up to 10 minutes per age category per day, a juvenile bronze dragon, along with creatures or vessels within 50 ft., can move at twice its normal speed in water."}],"description":"Bronze dragons have been known to ally with travelers and adventurers if the cause and reward is right and just.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mezlan","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"ooze","subtypes":["shapechanger"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":30,"ac_touch":18,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +1 dodge, +12 natural","hp":195,"hd":"17d8+119","hdvalue":17,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (acid)"],"fort":12,"ref":14,"will":11,"immunities":["ooze traits"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"climb","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":20}],"melee":"2 morphic weapons +22 (2d8+10)","ranged":"morphic weapon +19 (2d8+10)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (15 ft. with 1 slam per round)","special_attacks":[{"type":"sneak attack","details":"+3d6"},{"type":"spell battery","details":"chain lightning [DC 19], dispel magic, mage armor"}],"strength":30,"dexterity":25,"constitution":24,"intelligence":15,"wisdom":18,"charisma":17,"baseatk":12,"cmb":22,"cmd":40,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Point-Blank Shot"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Precise Shot"},{"feat":"Stealthy"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":15},{"skill":"Bluff","value":14},{"skill":"Climb","value":18},{"skill":"Disguise","value":25},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":9},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Stealth","value":25},{"skill":"Swim","value":18}],"languages":["Aklo","Azlanti","Common","versatile speech"],"sq":[{"type":"morphic body"},{"type":"skill pool"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"An amorphous blob coalesces, slowly rising up to form into a humanoid figure. As it stabilizes, intricate details emerge.","source":"AP 66","special_abilities":[{"type":"Morphic Body","kind":"Ex","details":"A mezlan can assume the appearance of any Medium or Small creature (other than creatures with the elemental, incorporeal, or swarm subtypes-the body assumed must be solid). The mezlan's creature type doesn't change in this new form and it gains none of the mimicked creature's special abilities; the transformation is cosmetic only. In these other forms, the mezlan retains all of its normal statistics and abilities as depicted above. Though this ability only affects the mezlan's outward image, it is a transmutation effect."},{"type":"Morphic Weapons","kind":"Ex","details":"A mezlan can manipulate its body to mimic a wide array of potent weaponry wielded by its various forms. While the weapons may look different, they are considered natural weapons and they all do the same amount of damage; are treated as magic for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction; and deal bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage. Once per round, a mezlan can extend one of its limbs to strike at a distance up to 15 ft. away with one of its slam attacks. Also, while mimicking a creature wielding a ranged weapon, a mezlan can fire a portion of its body as if the fragment were a projectile. This projectile is treated as a thrown weapon and has a range increment of 60 ft."},{"type":"Skill Pool","kind":"Ex","details":"A mezlan has a special knack for solving problems. Five times per day, it can apply a +4 competence bonus on any skill check, even checks for skills it has no ranks in or skills that can only be used untrained."},{"type":"Spell Battery","kind":"Su","details":"A mezlan can store up to 10 levels of spells that it can then cast freely. The spells imbued into a mezlan are each activated with the casting time for the relevant spell and are cast at the caster level of the spellcaster who provided the spells. A mezlan can store and use both divine and arcane spells, and can be imbued by any number of casters at a time. To fuel this ability, a caster must cast her spells into the mezlan; alternatively, the spellcaster can use a scroll to place a spell into the mezlan. A mezlan must voluntarily lower its spell resistance in order to be imbued with spells. In addition, a mezlan can choose to lower its spell resistance and absorb spells cast at it. The mezlan must be aware of the incoming spell and ready an action to absorb it. Only spells that have the mezlan as a target can be absorbed in this way; area spells are not absorbed. If a mezlan already possesses 10 levels of spells, it cannot absorb more. The mezlan can use these absorbed spells as its own."},{"type":"Versatile Speech","kind":"Ex","details":"A mezlan has a talent for parsing spoken languages. After spending 1 minute listening to a speaker use a language it doesn't already know, a mezlan can understand that language. After listening for 1 additional minute, the mezlan can speak the language. This understanding lasts for 24 hours before fading from the mezlan's mutable mind. To understand the same language again after this time, the mezlan must spend another minute listening to a creature speak that language. The mezlan doesn't have to be engaged in a conversation to use this ability."}],"description":"Built by Azlanti arcanists and engineers to perform the duties of spies and elite troops, units of mezlans were deployed to engage in extractions, infiltrations, and quick strikes on well-protected locations. Scholars believe that at the height of Azlant, close to 1,500 mezlans were created to save the empire. The difficulty of destroying mezlans leads scholars to believe that at least half of them still exist to this day.\n\nMezlans blur the lines between constructs and oozes, a mixture made even more strange by their possession of unique, previously human personalities. Each mezlan was once an exemplary living Azlanti or Thassilonian soldier graced with superior skills and intelligence. Upon being chosen for this new duty, these soldiers were given a full explanation of the changes they would undergo and signed a contract to serve them empire as mezlans. Each was then subjected to numerous magical and technological procedures to extract her consciousness, preserve it, and inject it into her new form. Sometimes the process didn't take as well as others, and resulted in an incomplete and flawed mezlan. Evidence of these flawed specimens didn't always reveal itself before the creatures were deployed, and many these became rogue mezlans.\n\nMost mezlans were recruited from the ranks of the military, and thus most of them possessed martial-related or skill-related class levels; however, a few of these creatures were once wizards who traded their magical talent for an amorphous form and near immortality.\n\nEcology\n\nWithout the need to eat, sleep, or breathe, mezlans are practically immortal. When they are defeated in battle, they simply discorporate and begin seeping down into the soil or cracks in the ground. If the material making up a mezlan isn't contained in some way or destroyed by subjecting it to continued energy damage, the creature lies dormant for 10 years before reforming. When a mezlan reincorporates, it is treated as if it had 16 negative levels. These negative levels are removed through time at a rate of 1 per month.\n\nMezlans retain a portion of their previous memories and experiences, but the extent of those memories varies from individual to individual. Some mezlans slowly regain their memories, some immediately remember everything from their previous incorporation, and others never fully grasp their previous selves.\n\nHabitat & Society\n\nMezlans seem to get along and work well with other mezlans, but to normal, living creatures, they appear strange and unnatural. They are very observant creatures who study everything they encounter, especially creatures-a frequent use of their skill pool ability. Some mezlans become accustomed to a particular form or body and use that persona as a default. Others enjoy keeping dozens of regular personas and cycle through them for particular duties they need to complete, meshing these personalities into a toolkit they use throughout their day-to-day activities. A few purists keep an amorphous, bloblike form unless they need to resemble something else. Strange mezlans who have gone mad over the years constantly shift their forms, flickering between hundreds of different ones.\n\nBecoming a Mezlan\n\nThough not constructs, mezlans are still created beings, the marriage of transformative magic and a living soul. Only the prohibitive cost of creating mezlans, not any shortage of volunteers, prevented their creators from manufacturing thousands of them. The sheer volume of djezet needed to create a mezlan forced their creators to grant the honor of the transformation to only the best of the best, greatly increasing their worth.\n\nThe method for creating a mezlan is lost to time, though it is rumored one of them retains the knowledge to produce more of its own kind. In any case, the price of the materials and special processes necessary to create an army of mezlans would likely bankrupt a nation.","ecology":"Without the need to eat, sleep, or breathe, mezlans are practically immortal. When they are defeated in battle, they simply discorporate and begin seeping down into the soil or cracks in the ground. If the material making up a mezlan isn't contained in some way or destroyed by subjecting it to continued energy damage, the creature lies dormant for 10 years before reforming. When a mezlan reincorporates, it is treated as if it had 16 negative levels. These negative levels are removed through time at a rate of 1 per month.\n\nMezlans retain a portion of their previous memories and experiences, but the extent of those memories varies from individual to individual. Some mezlans slowly regain their memories, some immediately remember everything from their previous incorporation, and others never fully grasp their previous selves.","habitat_society":"Mezlans seem to get along and work well with other mezlans, but to normal, living creatures, they appear strange and unnatural. They are very observant creatures who study everything they encounter, especially creatures-a frequent use of their skill pool ability. Some mezlans become accustomed to a particular form or body and use that persona as a default. Others enjoy keeping dozens of regular personas and cycle through them for particular duties they need to complete, meshing these personalities into a toolkit they use throughout their day-to-day activities. A few purists keep an amorphous, bloblike form unless they need to resemble something else. Strange mezlans who have gone mad over the years constantly shift their forms, flickering between hundreds of different ones.\n\nBecoming a Mezlan\n\nThough not constructs, mezlans are still created beings, the marriage of transformative magic and a living soul. Only the prohibitive cost of creating mezlans, not any shortage of volunteers, prevented their creators from manufacturing thousands of them. The sheer volume of djezet needed to create a mezlan forced their creators to grant the honor of the transformation to only the best of the best, greatly increasing their worth.\n\nThe method for creating a mezlan is lost to time, though it is rumored one of them retains the knowledge to produce more of its own kind. In any case, the price of the materials and special processes necessary to create an army of mezlans would likely bankrupt a nation."},{"name":"Mountain Troll","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CN","size":"Huge","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["giant"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":29,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +20 natural, -2 size","hp":207,"hd":"18d8+126","hdvalue":18,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (acid or fire)"],"fort":18,"ref":7,"will":15,"defensive_abilities":["rock catching","stubborn"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to sonic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":10},{"type":"climb","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +24 (2d10+13), 2 claws +24 (2d6+13)","ranged":"rock +13 (2d8+19)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 2d6+13"},{"type":"rock throwing","details":"120 ft."}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"stone shape"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"earthquake"},{"spell":"flesh to stone"},{"spell":"summon monster VIII","details":"earth elemental only"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"spike stones"},{"spell":"stone tell"}]}],"strength":36,"dexterity":13,"constitution":25,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":16,"charisma":8,"baseatk":13,"cmb":28,"cmd":39,"feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Deadly Aim"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Iron Will"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quick Draw"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":15}],"languages":["Giant"],"environments":["cold mountains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This enormous, stooped creature has powerful limbs; a mane of gritty brown fur; and a ferocious, tusked underbite.","group":"Troll","source":"Lands Of The Linnorm Kings","special_abilities":[{"type":"Stubborn","kind":"Ex","details":"A mountain troll gains a +4 racial bonus on all Will saving throws. In addition, if the troll fails a saving throw against a charm or compulsion effect, it can immediately attempt a second saving throw against the same effect on the next round to end the duration of the effect early."}],"description":"Though grotesque, charmless, and prone to fits of violence, mountain trolls are not inherently evil, nor do they always attack intruders on sight. A mountain troll prefers to withdraw and observe before entering combat, lumbering forth to attack only if intruders make clear their intentions to harm it or its allies, or if the newcomers seem to be encroaching upon the troll's territory rather than simply passing through. Once enraged, a mountain troll is a savage opponent, calling upon its native strength and alliances with elementals to bury its opponents in stone or spread their entrails across the slopes.\n\nMountain trolls prefer to live in narrow ravines or shallow caves that allow them to look out over the landscape. They sometimes knuckle-walk like a gorilla, but when angered they rear up to their full height of nearly 30 ft.\n\nMountain trolls have a close association with the First World, similar to that possessed by gnomes, which grants them magical abilities and unusual patience. They are quick to forge alliances with fey, and while they see smaller trolls as sadists, they nonetheless feel a sort of familial responsibility. Lesser trolls often capitalize upon mountain trolls' generosity, but take care to abide by their larger cousins' rules when sheltering in their homes. Mountain trolls have even been known to aid explorers or give advice, provided they are treated with respect.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mythic Elder Air Elemental","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","elemental","extraplanar","mythic"],"init":15,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":33,"ac_touch":20,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+11 Dex, +1 dodge, +13 natural, -2 size","hp":202,"hd":"16d10+114","hdvalue":16,"fort":14,"ref":21,"will":8,"defensive_abilities":["air mastery"],"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +25 (4d8+11 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"create vacuum"},{"type":"elevated ejection"},{"type":"fast swallow"},{"type":"mythic power","details":"5/day, surge +1d8"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"2d8+9 bludgeoning damage, AC 14, 20 hp, DR 10/-"},{"type":"whirlwind","details":"at will, 10-60 ft. high, 2d8+9 damage, DC 27"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":33,"constitution":18,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":13,"charisma":11,"baseatk":16,"cmb":27,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":49,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Iron Will","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse","type":"mythic"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":30},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":30},{"skill":"Fly","value":34},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Stealth","value":22}],"languages":["Auran"],"environments":["any (Plane of Air)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This living tornado draws in all the air that surrounds it, hurling unrestrained objects as it moves.","group":"Elemental","source":"Mythic Adventures","special_abilities":[{"type":"Air Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"Airborne creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against a mythic air elemental."},{"type":"Create Vacuum","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a mythic elder air elemental can suck the air out of the lungs of creatures it has swallowed or that are trapped in its whirlwind (Fortitude DC 27 negates). Creatures that fail the save take 2d6 points of damage and must attempt Constitution checks each round as if they had run out of breath. An affected character can't speak, use breath weapons, cast spells with verbal components, or do anything else that requires breathing. A trapped creature that succeeds at its save must succeed at a concentration check to cast spells. The air elemental can maintain this vacuum as a move action. If it stops, the trapped or swallowed creatures can breathe again. The save DC is Strength-based."},{"type":"Elevated Ejection","kind":"Ex","details":"When a mythic air elemental in whirlwind form ejects a trapped creature, it can do so from any point up to the whirlwind's current height, dropping the creature into the whirlwind's space or within the elemental's normal reach. The creature takes falling damage as normal. If the elemental expends one use of mythic power, it can instead throw a trapped creature as if using the uncanny grapple path ability with no grapple check needed."},{"type":"Swallow Whole","kind":"Ex","details":"A mythic air elemental can use this ability on a creature it has grabbed. If a trapped creature cuts itself free, the hole heals itself closed at the start of the elemental's next turn, allowing it to use swallow whole again."}],"description":"A mythic elder air elemental is pure fury and strength, capable of throwing wooden splinters through stone walls and tearing creatures apart with fists of solid wind. Its greatest speed is within its empty core, able to suffocate enemies in moments.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mythic Elder Earth Elemental","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar","mythic"],"init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":29,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":29,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +22 natural, -2 size","hp":218,"hd":"16d10+130","hdvalue":16,"fort":15,"ref":4,"will":11,"defensive_abilities":["trap weapon"],"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":20}],"speed_mod":"earth glide","melee":"2 slams +26 (4d6+18/18-20)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"earth mastery"},{"type":"mythic power","details":"5/day, surge +1d8"},{"type":"petrify"},{"type":"stun"},{"type":"trample","details":"4d6+18, DC 30"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"stone shape"}]},{"frequency":"5/day","spells":[{"spell":"transmute mud to rock"}]}],"strength":34,"dexterity":8,"constitution":21,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":13,"charisma":11,"baseatk":16,"cmb":30,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush or overrun, +2 vs. sunder","cmd":41,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, overrun, or sunder","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Greater Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (slam)","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Power Attack","type":"mythic"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":20},{"skill":"Climb","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10}],"languages":["Terran"],"sq":[{"type":"powerful blows","details":"slam"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Earth)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This humanoid mountain of stone and earth strides forward on legs like pillars, a vast grove covering its back.","group":"Elemental","source":"Mythic Adventures","special_abilities":[{"type":"Earth Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"A earth elemental gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls if both it and its foe are touching the ground. If an opponent is airborne or waterborne, the elemental takes a -4 penalty on attack and damage rolls. These modifiers apply to bull rush and overrun maneuvers, whether the elemental is initiating or resisting these kinds of attacks."},{"type":"Petrify","kind":"Su","details":"If it hits a target with a slam attack, a mythic earth elemental can expend two uses of mythic power to permanently turn that target to stone. If the target succeeds at a DC 23 Fortitude save, it is slowed (as the spell) for 1d6 rounds instead of petrified. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Stun","kind":"Ex","details":"If a mythic earth elemental strikes an opponent with two slams in 1 round, that creature must succeed at a DC 30 Fortitude save or be stunned for 1d6 rounds. The save DC is Strength-based."},{"type":"Trap Weapon","kind":"Ex","details":"A mythic earth elemental's body traps manufactured weapons that damage it. A manufactured weapon that deals hit point damage to the elemental (after subtracting its DR) is stuck fast unless the wielder succeeds at a DC 30 Reflex save. A creature can spend a standard action to attempt a DC 30 Strength check to remove a stuck weapon. Weapons that deal only bludgeoning damage are immune to this ability. The elemental can release any number of stuck weapons as a free action. The save DC is Strength-based."}],"description":"Infused with the power and wisdom of the deepest, oldest stone, a mythic elder earth elemental is a rocky bulwark against progress and change. They use innate magic and their very bodies to block enemy advances and preserve treasures of the earth.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mythic Elder Fire Elemental","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","fire","mythic"],"init":13,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["frightful presence (60 ft., DC 18)","shroud of flame (15 ft., 2d6 fire, DC 22)","smoke cloud (10 ft., DC 22)"],"ac":32,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+9 Dex, +2 dodge, +13 natural, -2 size","hp":202,"hd":"16d10+114","hdvalue":16,"fort":14,"ref":19,"will":8,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits","fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60}],"melee":"2 slams +23 (2d8+8 plus burn)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"blinding blaze"},{"type":"burn","details":"2d10, DC 22"},{"type":"inferno"},{"type":"mythic power","details":"5/day, surge +1d8"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"produce flame"}]},{"frequency":"5/day","spells":[{"spell":"flame arrow"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]}],"strength":26,"dexterity":29,"constitution":18,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":13,"charisma":11,"baseatk":16,"cmb":26,"cmd":47,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Dodge","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Iron Will","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Lightning Stance"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Wind Stance"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":28,"special":"+40 when jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":27},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":28},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":19},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20}],"languages":["Ignan"],"environments":["any (Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This blazing conflagration is vaguely humanoid in shape, its horned visage almost too bright to look upon.","group":"Elemental","source":"Mythic Adventures","special_abilities":[{"type":"Blinding Blaze","kind":"Su","details":"A mythic fire elemental can expend one use of mythic power as a swift action to burn brightly, granting it a blinding gaze attack. This gaze causes permanent blindness and has a range of 60 ft. A creature that succeeds at a DC 22 Fortitude save is instead dazzled for 1 round. Fire elementals are immune to this blindness. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Inferno","kind":"Ex","details":"A mythic fire elemental can expend one use of mythic power as an immediate action to lose its vulnerability to cold for 1 round. During this time, any fire damage it deals ignores fire resistance and fire immunity."},{"type":"Shroud of Flame","kind":"Ex","details":"Any creature within a mythic fire elemental's reach must succeed at a DC 22 Reflex save at the start of its turn or take 2d6 points of fire damage. The elemental can suppress or reactivate this ability at will as a free action. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Smoke Cloud","kind":"Ex","details":"As a swift action, a mythic fire elemental can create a choking cloud of smoke. This cloud is equivalent to that of pyrotechnics and lasts 1 minute. Fire elementals are immune to the effects of this ability."}],"description":"A mythic elder fire elemental is a living fragment of the original fires at the heart of its home plane. Having learned the patience of a slow burn, it lacks both the recklessness of younger fire elementals and the urge to inspire fear in the hearts of flammable mortals. It enjoys using smoke to scatter opponents so it can chase them down and set them alight.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mythic Elder Water Elemental","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","mythic","water"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":30,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +2 dodge, +14 natural, -2 size","hp":202,"hd":"16d10+114","hdvalue":16,"fort":14,"ref":18,"will":6,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":90}],"melee":"4 slams +24 (2d10+10/18-20 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"drench"},{"type":"fast swallow"},{"type":"mythic power","details":"5/day, surge +1d8"},{"type":"pressure wave"},{"type":"smother"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"2d10+10 bludgeoning damage, AC 14, 20 hp, DR 10/-"},{"type":"vortex","details":"at will, 10-60 ft., 2d10+10 damage, DC 28"},{"type":"water mastery"}],"strength":30,"dexterity":22,"constitution":19,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":13,"charisma":11,"baseatk":16,"cmb":28,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush or sunder, +4 vs. grapple","cmd":48,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush or sunder","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Dodge","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (slam)","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack","type":"mythic"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":25},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Stealth","value":17},{"skill":"Swim","value":37,"special":"."}],"languages":["Aquan"],"environments":["any (Plane of Water)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Thousands of gallons of water rise up to become a tentacled face, a bulbous body, and four long tentacular appendages.","group":"Elemental","source":"Mythic Adventures","special_abilities":[{"type":"Drench","kind":"Ex","details":"The elemental's touch puts out nonmagical flames of Large size or smaller. The creature can dispel magical fire it touches as dispel magic (caster level 16th)."},{"type":"Pressure Wave","kind":"Su","details":"A mythic water elemental can expend one use of mythic power to create a 60-foot-radius bust of pressurized water. Creatures in the area must attempt a DC 22 Fort save. Success means the creature is sickened for 1d4 rounds; failure means the creature is nauseated for 1d4 rounds and sickened for 1d4 rounds after that. If the elemental expends two uses of mythic power, creatures nauseated by this ability also take slam damage. Creatures with the aquatic or water subtypes are immune to this ability. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Swallow Whole","kind":"Ex","details":"The elemental can use this ability on a creature it has grabbed. If a trapped creature cuts itself free, the hole heals itself closed at the start of the elemental's next turn, allowing it to use swallow whole again."},{"type":"Vortex","kind":"Su","details":"A water elemental can create a whirlpool as a standard action, at will (as a whirlwind, but only underwater and cannot leave the water)."},{"type":"Water Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"If a water elemental and its opponent are touching water, the elemental gains a +1 bonus on attack rolls, damage rolls, and bull rush and overrun combat maneuver checks. If it or the opponent are touching the ground, the elemental takes a -4 penalty on attack rolls, on damage rolls, and to its CMD to resist bull rush and overrun attempts."}],"description":"A mythic water elemental comes from the unknowable depths of its home plane, predating the current civilizations and gods. A witness to ancient and bizarre acts of life-creation, it is unconcerned about the interests of mortal creatures.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Nalfeshnee","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"true seeing"}],"auras":["unholy aura (DC 23)"],"ac":29,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+4 deflection, +1 Dex, +16 natural, -2 size","hp":203,"hd":"14d10+126","hdvalue":14,"fort":22,"ref":9,"will":21,"dr":"10/good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +23 (3d8+11/19-20), 2 claws +23 (2d6+11)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"unholy nimbus"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"true seeing"},{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"call lightning"},{"spell":"feeblemind"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 lbs. of objects only"},{"spell":"slow"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 5, 1 nalfeshnee 20%, 1d4 hezrous 40%, or 1d4 vrocks 50%"}]}],"strength":32,"dexterity":13,"constitution":29,"intelligence":23,"wisdom":22,"charisma":20,"baseatk":14,"cmb":27,"cmd":42,"feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":22},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":22},{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":19},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (any one other)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":31},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":23},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":23},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":22}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Draconic","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","warband (1 nalfeshnee, 1 hezrou, and 2-5 vrocks)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"A towering, corpulent beast, this fiend has the hideous head of a boar and arms ending in fatty, four-fingered hands.","group":"Demon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Unholy Nimbus","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day as a free action a nalfeshnee can create a nimbus of unholy light, causing nauseating beams of writhing color to play around its body. One round later, the light bursts in a 60-foot radius. Any non-demon creature caught within this area must succeed on a DC 22 Will save or be dazed for 1d10 rounds as visions of madness hound it. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Few demons understand the inner workings of the Abyss like the nalfeshnee, and it isn't unusual to see a nalfeshnee seeming to serve the Abyss itself rather than a demon lord. Some claim stewardship over the fleshy realms that birth new demons, while others guard sites of particular significance deep in the plane's secret reaches. Often, a nalfeshnee's realm in the Abyss surpasses the strength and size of the largest of mortal kingdoms, for nalfeshnees display a singular gift for managing and ordering the chaos of the Abyss. Mortal summoners often seek them out for their unparalleled yet mad intellects, ever taking care to comb through bargains with such demons for hidden and unwanted consequences, for there is little a nalfeshnee will agree to do that doesn't, in some sinister way, advance the needs and desires of the Abyss. Nalfeshnees stand 20 ft. tall and weigh 8,000 pounds. They form from the souls of greedy or avaricious evil mortals, particularly those who ruled over empires of slavery, theft, banditry, and more violent vices.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Nightwing","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"undead","subtypes":["extraplanar","nightshade"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darksense"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["desecrating aura (30 ft.)"],"ac":29,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":25,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +17 natural, -2 size","hp":195,"hd":"17d8+119","hdvalue":17,"fort":12,"ref":11,"will":17,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["cold","undead traits"],"sr":25,"weaknesses":["light aversion"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +23 (4d10+18/19- 20 plus 4d6 cold and magic drain)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"channel energy","details":"7d6, DC 28, 8/day"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":14,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"magic fang"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"contagion"},{"spell":"deeper darkness"},{"spell":"unholy blight"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"cone of cold"},{"spell":"finger of death"},{"spell":"plane shift"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 6, 2 greater shadows"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"confusion"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"haste"},{"spell":"hold monster"},{"spell":"invisibility"}]}],"strength":31,"dexterity":18,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":21,"charisma":21,"baseatk":12,"cmb":24,"cmd":38,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Command Undead"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":25},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":25},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16,"special":"+24 in darkness"},{"skill":"Swim","value":27}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Negative Energy Plane)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","flight (3-6)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This enormous, bat-like creature is shaped from utter darkness, its eyes tiny red stars in the blackest night.","group":"Nightshade","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Magic Drain","kind":"Su","details":"The bite of a nightwing drains magical power and energy. When a nightwing bites a foe, the victim must make a DC 23 Will save or one spell effect currently affecting him immediately ends-determine which spell is drained randomly if the target is under the effects of more than one spell. The nightwing heals damage equal to twice the level of the spell drained-hit points in excess of its maximum are instead gained as temporary hit points that last for 1 hour. If a nightwing attempts to sunder a magic item with its bite, its magic-draining bite renders the item nonmagical for 1d4 rounds (if the item is a permanent magic item), drains 1d8 charges (if the item has charges), or renders it permanently nonmagical (if the item is a one-use item). The item (or its wielder, if the item is attended) can resist this effect with a DC 23 Will save. Damage dealt to an item is applied after the effects of magic drain are applied. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"The least of the known types of nightshade, the nightwing is nevertheless a deadly foe. Nightwings often serve more powerful nightshades as aerial support. These nightshades are also the most likely to be found serving a non-undead master-nightwings are often used by powerful mortals as guardians or sentinels. Despite this, nightwings still hope to someday slay any master they serve. They enter servitude primarily as a method of aiding a destructive or murderous mortal in their task of mass murder; once this task is over, or if at any point the nightwing believes its master is slacking in its murderous duties, the nightwing is swift to turn on its one-time ally.\n\nA nightwing found on the Material Plane not in the employ of a more powerful master is typically encountered in rugged terrain where there are numerous locations that can provide shelter when the sun rises. The monsters prefer caves and abandoned buildings for this purpose.\n\nA nightwing's body is 20 ft. long, but its wingspan is 80 ft. It weighs 4,500 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ocean Giant","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CG","size":"Huge","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["aquatic","giant"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":28,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+20 natural, -2 size","hp":218,"hd":"19d8+133","hdvalue":19,"fort":18,"ref":8,"will":10,"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":30},{"type":"electricity","value":30}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"mwk trident +29 (3d6+22) or 2 slams +27 (2d6+15)","ranged":"rock +13 (2d8+22)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"conch focus"},{"type":"rock throwing","details":"110 ft."}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"freedom of movement"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"vortex"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"aqueous orb"},{"spell":"control winds"},{"spell":"shout"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally VII","details":"swimming creatures only"},{"spell":"water breathing"}]}],"strength":40,"dexterity":11,"constitution":25,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":18,"baseatk":14,"cmb":31,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","cmd":41,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","feats":[{"feat":"Augment SummoningB (with conch)"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Martial Weapon Proficiency (trident)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (trident)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":17},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Perform (wind)","value":13},{"skill":"Survival","value":14},{"skill":"Swim","value":24}],"languages":["Aquan","Common","Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"}],"environments":["any oceans"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-5)","family (2-5 plus 35% noncombatants and 1 druid or sorcerer of 4th-7th level)"],"treasure":"standard (mwk trident)","description_visual":"This blue-skinned giant's clothing and beard whip about like sails caught in a storm.","group":"Giant","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Conch Focus","kind":"Su","details":"When holding its conch, an ocean giant can cast great shout (DC 22) instead of shout, and gains Augment Summoning as a bonus feat. If the conch is destroyed (hardness 5, 20 hp), the giant can spend 1 week to craft a replacement."}],"description":"Ocean giants embody the great extremes of the sea. Their skin colors vary from deep blue to pale green, and their eyes and hair range from foamy white to coral pink. They decorate themselves with the treasures of the sea, wearing shell jewelry or scrimshaw, and clothing woven from underwater plants, or even salvaged sails. Each ocean giant carries a hand-crafted musical horn made from a conch shell, an object of cultural significance representing its family history and travels on the vast sea. Many ocean giants view themselves as guardians of the sea, its creatures, and those who travel the waves, safeguarding their charges from remarkable coral towers. Others, however, claim domains measuring thousands of leagues, enslaving the beasts and aquatic races within and shattering any ship that dares trespass near their citadels of urchins and bones. Adult ocean giants stand approximately 22 ft. tall and weigh about 15,000 pounds. Most live to be about 500 years old.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Old Black Dragon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (240 ft., DC 22)"],"ac":32,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+24 natural, -2 size","hp":225,"hd":"18d12+108","hdvalue":18,"fort":17,"ref":11,"will":15,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["acid","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"Bite +26 (2d8+13 plus 2d6 acid), 2 claws +25 (2d6+9), 2 wings +23 (1d8+4), tail +23 (2d6+13)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"acidic bite"},{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 25, 16d6 acid"},{"type":"corrupt water"},{"type":"crush","details":"2d8+13"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":18,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"darkness","details":"80-ft. radius"},{"spell":"plant growth"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":13,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"heroism"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"glitterdust"},{"spell":"summon swarm"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":29,"dexterity":10,"constitution":23,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":19,"charisma":16,"baseatk":18,"cmb":29,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":21},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19},{"skill":"Swim","value":38}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Giant","Orc"],"environments":["warm marshes"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Hissing green acid drips from the fanged maw of this black-scaled, horned dragon.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acidic Bite","kind":"Su","details":"At old age, a black dragon's bite deals an additional 2d6 points of acid damage. An ancient dragon's damage increases to 4d6, and a great wrym's to 6d6."},{"type":"Corrupt Water","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day an adult or older black dragon can stagnate 10 cubic ft. of still water, making it foul and unable to support water-breathing life. The ability spoils liquids containing water. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC equal to the dragon's frightful presence) or become ruined. This ability is the equivalent of a 1st-level spell. Its range is equal to that of the dragon's frightful presence."},{"type":"Crush","kind":"Ex","details":"A flying or jumping Huge or larger dragon can land on foes as a standard action, using its whole body to crush them. Crush attacks are effective only against opponents three or more size categories smaller than the dragon. A crush attack affects as many creatures as fit in the dragon's space. Creatures in the affected area must succeed on a Reflex save (DC equal to that of the dragon's breath weapon) or be pinned, automatically taking bludgeoning damage during the next round unless the dragon moves off them. If the dragon chooses to maintain the pin, it must succeed at a combat maneuver check as normal. Pinned foes take damage from the crush each round if they don't escape. A crush attack deals the indicated damage plus 1-1/2 times the dragon's Strength bonus."},{"type":"Speak with Reptiles","kind":"Sp","details":"A young or older black dragon gains the constant spell-like ability to speak with reptiles. This functions as speak with animals, but only with reptilian animals."},{"type":"Swamp Stride","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older black dragon can move through bogs and quicksand without penalty at its normal speed."},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A black dragon can breathe underwater indefinitely and can freely use its breath weapon, spells, and other abilities while submerged."}],"description":"Lording over the darkest swamps and marshes, black dragons are the undisputed masters of their domain, ruling through cruelty and intimidation. Those who dwell within a black dragon's reach live in fear. Black dragons tend to make their lairs in remote parts of the swamp, preferably in caves at the bottom of dark and fetid pools. Inside, they pile up their filthy treasure and sleep amid the roots and muck. Black dragons prefer their food a bit rotten and will often allow a meal to sit in a pool for days before consuming it. Black dragons prefer treasures that don't rot or decay, making their hoard, full of coins, gemstones, jewelry, and other objects made from stone or metal.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Old Brass Dragon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"CG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["fire"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"blindsense","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["fire (5 ft., 1d6 fire)","frightful presence (240 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":32,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+24 natural, -2 size","hp":225,"hd":"18d12+108","hdvalue":18,"fort":17,"ref":11,"will":15,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":25,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"burrow","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +25 (2d8+13), 2 claws +25 (2d6+9), 2 wings +23 (1d8+4), tail slap +23 (2d6+13)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft. (20 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 25, 16d4 fire"},{"type":"crush","details":"small creatures, DC 25, 2d8+13"},{"type":"desert wind"},{"type":"sleep breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":18,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"control winds"},{"spell":"endure elements"},{"spell":"speak with animals"},{"spell":"suggestion"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":11,"spellsknown_concentration":17,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"mirage arcana"},{"spell":"prying eyes"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"confusion"},{"spell":"locate creature"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"displacement"},{"spell":"heroism"},{"spell":"hold person"},{"spell":"tongues"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alter self"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"resist energy"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"protection from evil"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"ventriloquism"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane mark"},{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"detect poison"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":29,"dexterity":10,"constitution":23,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":19,"charisma":18,"baseatk":18,"cmb":29,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Greater Spell Focus (enchantment)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Spell Focus (enchantment)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":25},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":25},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Heal","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":25},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":29},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":25},{"skill":"Survival","value":25}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","any 22"],"sq":[{"type":"move sand"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"A crest of horns sweeps back from the head of this dragon, leading to a long neck and serpentine brass body.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Desert Wind","kind":"Su","details":"A juvenile or older brass dragon can call up the desert wind to serve him. This functions as gust of wind, but any creature in its path must make a Fortitude save (DC 25) or be blinded for 1d4 rounds by the sand."},{"type":"Fire Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older brass dragon is surrounded by an aura of intense heat. All creatures within 5 ft. of the dragon take 1d6 points of fire damage at the beginning of the dragon's turn. An ancient brass dragon's aura extends to 10 ft. A great wyrm's damage increases to 2d6. A brass dragon can suppress or activate this aura at will as a free action."},{"type":"Move Sand","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older brass dragon can move sand to excavate ruins or hide treasures. This functions as move earth, but it only affects sand. The dragon uses his HD in place of his caster level for this effect. This is equivalent to a 5th-level spell."},{"type":"Sleep Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of fire, a brass dragon can breathe a 50 ft. cone of sleep gas. Creatures within the cone must succeed on a Will save or fall asleep for 1d6+8 rounds."}],"description":"Consummate conversationalists, brass dragons prefer to talk instead of fight. Brass dragons lair near humanoid settlements, where they can hear the most recent news and gossip.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Old Underworld Dragon","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["fire"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"smoke vision"}],"auras":["frightful presence (240 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":33,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":33,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +26 natural, -2 size","hp":225,"hd":"18d12+108","hdvalue":18,"fort":17,"ref":10,"will":15,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":25,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +27 (2d8+15/19-20), 2 claws +27 (2d6+10/19-20), gore +26 (2d6+15), tail slap +21 (2d6+15)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite and gore)","special_attacks":[{"type":"adamantine claws"},{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, 16d6 fire damage, DC 25"},{"type":"crush","details":"DC 25, 2d8+15"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":18,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"soften earth and stone"},{"spell":"spike stones"},{"spell":"stone shape"},{"spell":"wall of stone"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":9,"spellsknown_concentration":15,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"shout"},{"spell":"stone shape"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"displacement"},{"spell":"fireball"},{"spell":"protection from good"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"acid arrow"},{"spell":"flaming sphere"},{"spell":"resist energy"},{"spell":"scorching ray"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"cause fear"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"ray of enfeeblement"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"bleed"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"flare"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":31,"dexterity":8,"constitution":23,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":19,"charisma":18,"baseatk":18,"cmb":30,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite, claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Armor"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite, claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":25},{"skill":"Bluff","value":25},{"skill":"Climb","value":31},{"skill":"Fly","value":12},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering, geography, planes)","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":25},{"skill":"Stealth","value":18}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Dwarven","Ignan","Terran"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape"},{"type":"underworld burrower"}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This serpentine dragon has skin the color of deep volcanic rock, enormous claws, and jagged, stonelike horns and scales.","group":"Imperial Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Adamantine Claws","kind":"Ex","details":"The claws of an underworld dragon are made of adamantine, and have the qualities of a weapon made from that material."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older underworld dragon can assume any humanoid form three times per day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Smoke Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young and older underworld dragon can see perfectly in smoky conditions (such as those created by pyrotechnics)."},{"type":"Underworld Burrower","kind":"Ex","details":"An adult underworld dragon gains a 10-foot bonus to its burrow speed. When the underworld dragon becomes old and every two age categories thereafter, its burrow speed increases by an additional 10 ft."}],"description":"Underworld dragons, also called futsanglungs, are calculating, greedy creatures that carve great labyrinthine tunnels beneath the world, defending their hidden treasures. Preferring the earth to the heavens, they channel the fires of the world's core within their twisting, stonelike bodies and through flaming breath hot enough to turn granite into slag.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Peri","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"NG","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["good","native"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"smoke sight"}],"ac":30,"ac_touch":18,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +1 dodge, +12 natural","hp":180,"hd":"19d10+76","hdvalue":19,"fort":12,"ref":18,"will":17,"dr":"10/cold iron and evil","immunities":["electricity","fire"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":90,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+2 flaming burst scimitar +27 (1d6+8/18-20 plus 1d6 fire), 2 wings +20 (1d6+3 plus burn)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn","details":"2d6, DC 23"},{"type":"whirlwind dance"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":19,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"fire shield","details":"warm shield"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"aid"},{"spell":"flame jump"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"},{"spell":"scorching ray"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"fireball"},{"spell":"flame strike"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]}],"strength":22,"dexterity":24,"constitution":19,"intelligence":21,"wisdom":19,"charisma":26,"baseatk":19,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. disarm","cmd":43,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. disarm","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Disarm"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Whirlwind Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":29},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":30},{"skill":"Fly","value":33},{"skill":"Heal","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":26},{"skill":"Perform (any one)","value":30},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":26},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":29}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","Elven","Ignan","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any good-aligned plane"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"triple (+2 flaming burst scimitar)","description_visual":"This beautiful albino woman is wreathed in wings of brilliant flame.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Flame Jump","kind":"Sp","details":"A peri can enter any fire equal to the peri's size or larger and travel any distance to another fire in a single round, regardless of the distance between the two. This ability otherwise functions as greater teleport (caster level 14th), but the peri can transport only itself and up to 50 pounds of objects."},{"type":"Smoke Sight","kind":"Su","details":"A peri can see through fire, fog, and smoke without penalty."},{"type":"Whirlwind Dance","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day as a full-round action, a peri can spin in an ever-faster, whirling dance, transforming itself into a spinning vortex of flame 10 to 40 ft. high for up to 9 rounds. This ability functions as the whirlwind ability (DC 26 Reflex save), but any creature that comes in contact with the whirlwind or is caught inside it takes 2d6+6 points of fire damage and is subject to the peri's burn special attack. The save DC is Dexterity-based."}],"description":"Peris are a race of celestials native to the good-aligned Outer Planes, but they are also often found in the company of mortals on the Material Plane. Believed to be the descendants of fallen angels, peris do penance for their ancestors' sins before they can earn a place in paradise. As a result, peris work tirelessly to aid and support good heroes of the mortal realms in a never-ending battle against evil.\n\nPeris hate the evil fiends known as divs, who constantly seek to ruin the good works of mortals. Peris often work to repair damage wrought by the destructive divs. For their part, the divs take great pleasure in tormenting and persecuting peris, locking the fiery-winged celestials in cages of cold iron and endlessly torturing them.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Rokurokubi","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"monstrous humanoid","init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["nightfall (15 ft.)"],"ac":28,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +12 natural","hp":195,"hd":"17d10+102","hdvalue":17,"fort":11,"ref":16,"will":13,"dr":"5/cold iron","immunities":["sleep"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +24 (2d6+4/19-20 plus rokurokubi's curse), 2 claws +23 (1d6+4)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (20 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"elongate neck"},{"type":"rokurokubi's curse"}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":12,"spellsknown_concentration":22,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":3,"spells":[{"spell":"permanent image"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"feeblemind"},{"spell":"nightmare"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"confusion"},{"spell":"locate creature"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"fly"},{"spell":"keen edge"},{"spell":"wind wall"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"ghoul touch"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"knock"},{"spell":"touch of idiocy"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"disguise self"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shocking grasp"},{"spell":"sleep"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane mark"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"detect poison"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"open/close"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":23,"constitution":22,"intelligence":15,"wisdom":12,"charisma":21,"baseatk":17,"cmb":21,"cmd":37,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":26},{"skill":"Climb","value":24},{"skill":"Disguise","value":26},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":21},{"skill":"Stealth","value":26}],"languages":["Aklo","Common"],"sq":[{"type":"no sleep"}],"environments":["any ruins"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","harem (3-6)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This peasant woman sprouts a grotesquely long neck that coils about like a snake, with razor-sharp teeth filling her gaping maw.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Elongate Neck","kind":"Ex","details":"A rokurokubi can stretch her neck from a normal human length up to 20 ft., giving her reach with her bite attack and threatening all squares within that range."},{"type":"Nightfall Aura","kind":"Su","details":"A rokurokubi can create an aura of darkness and silence (CL 12th) with a radius of 15 ft. The rokurokubi is immune to the effects of her aura, and can activate or suppress this ability as a free action. These aura effects can be dispelled as if they were spells."},{"type":"No Sleep","kind":"Ex","details":"A rokurokubi doesn't need to sleep and is immune to all sleep effects."},{"type":"Rokurokubi's Curse","kind":"Su","details":"Bite-injury; save Will DC 23; frequency 1 day; effect 1 Cha damage and permanently silenced after 4 Cha damage. Fully healing the Cha damage cures the silence. The save DC is Charisma-based. Spells A rokurokubi casts spells as a 12th-level sorcerer."}],"description":"A rokurokubi is an evil hag-like creature who seeks to spread as much mayhem and despair as possible. Her skin ranges in hue from pale blue to muted green, so to disguise herself she must cover up her flesh with makeup and clothing, and retract her neck so it is no longer than a human's. A rokurokubi can mate with almost any male humanoid, monstrous humanoid, or humanoid-shaped creature. Her offspring is always a rokurokubi. The mate is usually devoured once the rokurokubi tires of his presence.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Sepid","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["div","evil","extraplanar"],"init":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":32,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +18 natural, -1 size","hp":202,"hd":"15d10+120","hdvalue":15,"fort":13,"ref":16,"will":15,"dr":"10/cold iron and good","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10}],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"+1 falchion +23 (2d6+11/15-20) or 2 claws +21 (1d6+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"rain of debris"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":23,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"deeper darkness"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 lbs. of objects only"},{"spell":"nondetection"},{"spell":"speak with dead"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"baleful polymorph"},{"spell":"bestow curse"},{"spell":"break enchantment"},{"spell":"create undead"},{"spell":"disintegrate"},{"spell":"enervation"},{"spell":"fireball"},{"spell":"hold monster"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 4, 1 ghawwas or 1 shira 40%"},{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"blindness/deafness"},{"spell":"fly"},{"spell":"ice storm"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"mirror image"},{"spell":"scorching ray"},{"spell":"touch of idiocy"},{"spell":"true strike"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":20,"constitution":27,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":19,"charisma":22,"baseatk":15,"cmb":23,"cmd":38,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deflect Arrows","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (falchion)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (falchion)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":24},{"skill":"Fly","value":15},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":19},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":22},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":24}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"deflect rays"}],"environments":["any (Abaddon)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard (+1 falchion)","description_visual":"Twice the height of a human, this horned monstrous warrior wields a massive blade.","group":"Div","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Deflect Rays","kind":"Su","details":"Once per round as an immediate action, a sepid can use its Deflect Arrows feat to deflect a ray or a spell that uses a ranged touch attack."},{"type":"Rain of Debris","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day as a standard action, a sepid can call forth a hail of stones, wood, metal, and similar debris. The debris rains down and pelts all creatures in a 10-foot-high, 40-foot-radius cylinder centered on the sepid, dealing 15d6 points of bludgeoning damage (Reflex DC 25 half). This attack doesn't harm the sepid, and counts as an evil attack for the purpose of damage reduction. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Warlords among the divs, sepids spread fear, slaughter, and despair wherever they pass. They foster battles, incite rebellions, and seek heroes to slay, destroying all that which gives common people hope. With their falchions in hand, sepids often stand at the fore of the foul legions they raise.\n\nSepids delight in twisting the truth, but while all divs are liars, sepids make themselves predictable by always doing the opposite of what they claim, and wise opponents turn this knowledge to their own advantage.\n\nSepids stand 13 ft. tall and weigh upward of 1,500 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Sphinx Colossus","cr":14,"xp":38400,"alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"construct","subtypes":["colossus","mythic"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"120 ft."},{"type":"x-ray vision"}],"auras":["frightful presence (150 ft., DC 20)","selective antimagic (20 ft.)"],"ac":31,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":30,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +24 natural, -4 size","hp":199,"hd":"18d10+100","hdvalue":18,"fort":6,"ref":9,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["block attacks","fortification (50%)"],"dr":"10/epic","immunities":["construct traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"speed_mod":"sand glide","melee":"2 slams +29 (3d6+15) or   stomp +29 (6d6+22 plus pinning stomp)","ranged":"rock +15 (3d6+15)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"mythic power","details":"4/day, surge +1d8"},{"type":"rock throwing","details":"120 ft."}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":12,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"moment of prescience"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"quickened true strike"}]}],"strength":40,"dexterity":13,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":15,"charisma":13,"baseatk":18,"cmb":37,"cmd":48,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":9},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":13}],"languages":["Ancient Osiriani","Sphinx"],"sq":[{"type":"alternate form"},{"type":"create rocks"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This towering stone edifice resembles a lion with a regal but blank human face.","group":"Sphinx","source":"Osirion, Legacy Of Pharaohs","special_abilities":[{"type":"Alternate Form","kind":"Ex","details":"As a full-round action, a sphinx colossus can take the form of a sphinx statue. Its DR increases to 20/epic, and it gains fast healing 10. While in this form, the colossus cannot attack or move, but it can use its spell-like and supernatural abilities. It can resume its base form as a full-round action."},{"type":"Create Rocks","kind":"Ex","details":"As a move action, a sphinx colossus can scoop up earth or rubble from an unoccupied square within its reach and compact it into a solid mass appropriate for use with its rock throwing ability."},{"type":"Selective Antimagic Aura","kind":"Su","details":"Spells and abilities of the divination school are unaffected by this aura."}],"description":"Relics carved by mythic priests and god-kings of Ancient Osirion, sphinx colossi stand roughly 60 ft. tall and weigh about 220,000 pounds.\n\nConstruction\n\nThe body of a sphinx colossus is first carved from sandstone of the highest quality costing 25,000 gp.\n\nSPHINX COLOSSUS\n\nCL 11th; Price 100,000 gp\n\nConstruction\n\nRequirements Craft Construct, Mythic Crafter, Quicken Spell, 4th mythic tier, antimagic field, limited wish, moment of prescience, true strike; Skill Craft (stonemasonry) DC 25; Cost 50,000 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
